# Run outputs and regenerable artefacts
runs/*
figures/

# ...except the compact evidence Sol reviews (D-062). A manifest that cannot
# reach the bundle cannot be checked by the reviewer it was written for, and
# these two files carry the run and member counts, the normalisation vectors
# and every artefact digest in 64 KB. The bulky run records, transition exports
# and figures they account for stay untracked and regenerable.
#
# Each level is unwound explicitly: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so "runs/" followed by an exception silently does
# nothing -- which is how this was first written, and it looked right.
!runs/w3_pilot/
runs/w3_pilot/*
!runs/w3_pilot/attempt-*/
runs/w3_pilot/attempt-*/*
!runs/w3_pilot/attempt-*/manifest.json
!runs/w3_pilot/attempt-*/rows.json
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# Environment
.venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Local Claude Code settings (machine-specific permissions)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code rewrites this file in place and leaves temp copies behind. They
# are machine-local and never project state -- but left untracked they make
# every sol_bundle.sh report DIRTY, and a dirty flag that is always on is a
# dirty flag nobody reads (D-036).
.claude/settings.local.json*

# Generated verification bundles. They live in the repo root so the student can
# find them, but a bundle that dirties the tree makes its own "tree: clean" line
# read DIRTY -- and a dirty flag that is always on is a dirty flag nobody reads.
sol_bundle*.txt
SOL_BUNDLE.txt
# The evidence archive for Sol (D-106). Generated by scripts/sol_evidence_archive.sh
# from the COMMIT OBJECT, so it is a deterministic function of tracked bytes and
# tracking it would duplicate 136 files already in the repository. Regenerate with
# the script; it rebuilds byte-identically and prints its own SHA-256.
SOL_THRESHOLD_EVIDENCE.tar.gz
bundle*.txt

# The W4 gate's evidence, tracked in full (D-074). The pilot tracks only its
# manifest and rows; the gate tracks the run records and metric streams too,
# because the evidence contract's trust boundary IS those digests -- untracked,
# a fresh clone could read the manifest's claims but verify none of them. The
# whole rung-0 attempt is 1.5 MB.
!runs/w4_gate/
runs/w4_gate/*
!runs/w4_gate/rung-*/
runs/w4_gate/rung-*/*
!runs/w4_gate/rung-*/verdict-attempt-*.json
!runs/w4_gate/rung-*/attempt-*/
runs/w4_gate/rung-*/attempt-*/*
!runs/w4_gate/rung-*/attempt-*/manifest.json
!runs/w4_gate/rung-*/attempt-*/rows.json
!runs/w4_gate/rung-*/attempt-*/records/
runs/w4_gate/rung-*/attempt-*/records/*
!runs/w4_gate/rung-*/attempt-*/records/*/
!runs/w4_gate/rung-*/attempt-*/records/*/run.json
!runs/w4_gate/rung-*/attempt-*/records/*/metrics.jsonl

# W4 Friday's TIMING evidence (D-116). Same shape as the gate's and the
# threshold's rules, and added for the same reason: `runs/*` swallows any new
# experiment directory silently, so a commit can claim to track evidence and
# ship none. That is the D-041 shape and it has now been caught THREE times --
# D-103 by inspection, D-116 by checking again before committing. The timing
# verdict is a Gate 1 input; digests and prose without the record are not
# auditable evidence.
!runs/w4_timing/
runs/w4_timing/*
!runs/w4_timing/attempt-*/
runs/w4_timing/attempt-*/*
!runs/w4_timing/attempt-*/timing.json
!runs/w4_timing/attempt-*/SUPERSEDED.md

# W4 Friday's threshold calibration (D-103). Same shape as the gate's rules and
# for the same reason (D-075 ruling 3): digests without files cannot be verified
# from a fresh clone, so the artefacts the threshold is recomputed from are
# tracked. Written only after the calibration ran and the commit that claimed to
# track the evidence turned out not to -- `runs/*` swallows any new experiment
# directory silently, which is the hazard the comment at the top of this file
# describes and which nothing enforces.
!runs/w4_threshold/
runs/w4_threshold/*
!runs/w4_threshold/attempt-*/
runs/w4_threshold/attempt-*/*
!runs/w4_threshold/attempt-*/threshold_calibration.json
!runs/w4_threshold/attempt-*/arrays/
!runs/w4_threshold/attempt-*/arrays/*.npy
!runs/w4_threshold/attempt-*/records/
runs/w4_threshold/attempt-*/records/*
!runs/w4_threshold/attempt-*/records/*/
!runs/w4_threshold/attempt-*/records/*/run.json
!runs/w4_threshold/attempt-*/records/*/metrics.jsonl
